        <terms:source>ISO 80000-1:2009 Quantities and units - Part 1: General, clause 3.6</terms:source>
        <rdfs:label>International System of Quantities</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>system of quantities based on the seven base quantities: length, mass, time, electric current, thermodynamic temperature, amount of substance, and luminous intensity</skos:definition>
        <skos:note>The International System of Units (SI) is based on the ISQ.</skos:note>
        <skos:note>This system of quantities is published in the ISO 80000 and IEC 80000 series Quantities and units, Parts 3 to 14.</skos:note>
        <AnnotationVocabulary:abbreviation>ISQ</AnnotationVocabulary:abbreviation>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


